# Starting linking on the local stack (docker compose up --wait), through the gateway.
# Sign in first, headless, as an unlinked login: scripts/dev-login.sh customer-c
# then copy the disputedesk-session value from the cookie jar it prints into @session below.
# Run "Antiforgery token" first: it sets the disputedesk-antiforgery cookie, so copy that value into @antiforgery.
# Every well-formed start answers 202 with an empty body, whatever the details; the job then checks them off the
# request path, and only a match with no linked login whose SIM-swap check passes gets an OTP, in Mailpit
# (http://localhost:8025). LinkingChallenges stores only the OTP's HMAC; AuditLogEntries records each stop.
# With curl, keep both cookies in the jar:
#   token=$(curl -s -b <jar> -c <jar> http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bff/antiforgery | jq -r .requestToken)
#   curl -i -b <jar> -H "X-XSRF-TOKEN: $token" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"idNumber":"8804125123080","accountNumber":"1000000041"}' http://localhost:8080/api/v1/linking/start

@app = http://localhost:8080
@session = paste-the-disputedesk-session-cookie-value
@antiforgery = paste-the-disputedesk-antiforgery-cookie-value

### Antiforgery token: the X-XSRF-TOKEN value for unsafe requests
# @name token
GET {{app}}/api/v1/bff/antiforgery
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### Customer D's details (not linked, passes every check): 202, and the OTP lands in Mailpit for +27820000004
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/start
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"idNumber": "8804125123080", "accountNumber": "1000000041"}

### Details that match no customer: the same 202; the job audits LinkingNoMatch and sends nothing
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/start
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"idNumber": "8804125123080", "accountNumber": "1000000049"}

### Customer C's details (recent SIM swap): the same 202; the job audits LinkingSimSwapFailed and sends nothing
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/start
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"idNumber": "9202295801081", "accountNumber": "1000000031"}

### An ID number with a wrong check digit: 400 validation naming idNumber, without the value
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/start
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"idNumber": "8804125123081", "accountNumber": "1000000041"}

### Verify the OTP from Mailpit (the latest message to +27820000004): 204 with an empty body links the login to
### customer D, and the same session cookie then reaches /api/v1/transactions. A wrong code answers 422 otp-incorrect
### with attemptsRemaining; three wrong codes answer 409 linking-locked, and the person starts linking again.
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/verify
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "paste-the-six-digit-otp"}

### A code of five digits: 400 validation naming code, without the value; no attempt is counted
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/verify
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "12345"}

### Rate limits: starts and verifies together allow 5 requests per login and 20 per client IP in a 15-minute sliding
### window, and a 400 counts too. Send this a sixth time within 15 minutes of the login's first linking request:
### 429 rate-limited with Retry-After: 900, one body for either limit; the first rejection per login or IP in a window
### is audited as LinkingRateLimited.
POST {{app}}/api/v1/linking/verify
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "12345"}
